hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2739","Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, who narrated to us Jarir, on the authority of Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (RA), who raised the narration to the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," circumambulation of the Sacred House (the Kaaba) is like prayer"," except that you are permitted to speak during it. So whoever speaks during it must only speak that which is good.\"" Abu Bakr (RA) reported: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered the guide of a man who was walking with difficulty"," being pulled along by his guide"," to lead him by the hand while he was performing circumambulation of the Sacred House. This narration falls under the chapter of good speech during circumambulation"," and I have also extracted it in another chapter."""
